1
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:43,960
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:46,950
[Episode 25]

3
00:01:46,979 --> 00:01:49,690
[Xiaoximen Hospital
Affiliated with Qikang Medical]

4
00:01:48,310 --> 00:01:49,240
So the three of us

5
00:01:49,350 --> 00:01:50,550
are a team from now on?

6
00:01:51,039 --> 00:01:51,870
You bet.

7
00:01:53,229 --> 00:01:54,560
Everything's changed.

8
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:56,039
Even Dr. Che's been let go.

9
00:01:57,310 --> 00:01:58,509
Chief Physician Liu,

10
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:00,500
we're counting on you from now on.

11
00:02:01,710 --> 00:02:03,950
From now on, everything will be managed
at the group level.

12
00:02:03,950 --> 00:02:06,210
Is being the hospital president any fun?

13
00:02:06,510 --> 00:02:07,350
I used to get

14
00:02:07,350 --> 00:02:09,240
four or five hours of sleep a night.

15
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:10,120
Now that I'm president,

16
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:11,470
I'm lucky

17
00:02:11,470 --> 00:02:12,360
if I get two.

18
00:02:12,750 --> 00:02:14,280
It's because I keep worrying
about all these things.

19
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:15,430
The more I think about it,
the harder it gets.

20
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:16,520
So I've decided
to stop thinking about it.

21
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:18,400
Let them criticize me all they want.

22
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:20,030
The number of available positions
is limited.

23
00:02:20,030 --> 00:02:21,360
What am I supposed to do?

24
00:02:21,910 --> 00:02:24,520
Liu, Tong, and Sun

25
00:02:24,710 --> 00:02:25,970
have all come to see me.

26
00:02:26,310 --> 00:02:27,370
What did they want?

27
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:32,310
They wanted to know why you were
made hospital president.

28
00:02:32,310 --> 00:02:33,800
So I explained

29
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:35,240
your predicament to them.

30
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:36,440
Guess what they said?

31
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:40,690
They must have thought being
hospital president wasn't that hard.

32
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:42,280
Director Yan

33
00:02:43,590 --> 00:02:44,800
can't interfere

34
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:47,470
with the company's internal management,
of course.

35
00:02:47,470 --> 00:02:48,840
But he did hint

36
00:02:48,870 --> 00:02:50,530
that I couldn't be president.

37
00:02:52,190 --> 00:02:53,079
So I had to pick someone

38
00:02:53,079 --> 00:02:54,610
I could keep under control.

39
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:57,600
I needed to secure that position first.

40
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:58,800
You...

41
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:01,300
You really don't mince words, do you?

42
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,870
Okay, I'm easy to manage.

43
00:03:04,150 --> 00:03:05,680
I'll do whatever you say.

44
00:03:05,870 --> 00:03:06,590
You know

45
00:03:06,590 --> 00:03:08,310
why I didn't pick Tong or the others?

46
00:03:08,310 --> 00:03:11,240
Because I'm deeply attached
to Xiaoximen Hospital.

47
00:03:11,430 --> 00:03:13,150
They're just as attached to it.

48
00:03:13,150 --> 00:03:14,550
Well, then I have no idea.

49
00:03:19,590 --> 00:03:21,710
Because you're a laid-back kind of guy.

50
00:03:21,710 --> 00:03:22,400
What?

51
00:03:22,470 --> 00:03:23,960
You know how to avoid trouble.

52
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:24,750
That's true.

53
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:31,040
Once all the people appointed
by the group arrive,

54
00:03:31,310 --> 00:03:32,310
the hospital

55
00:03:32,310 --> 00:03:33,470
will inevitably split into two camps:

56
00:03:33,470 --> 00:03:35,130
the locals and the outsiders.

57
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:41,600
When a powerful newcomer
clashes with the local establishment,

58
00:03:42,470 --> 00:03:43,800
they're bound

59
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:46,000
to fight over every little advantage.

60
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:47,590
Caught in the middle,

61
00:03:47,590 --> 00:03:49,430
you'll have an even harder time
than you do now.

62
00:03:49,430 --> 00:03:50,630
That's a tough one.

63
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:53,280
But as long as you stay calm,

64
00:03:54,030 --> 00:03:56,079
don't worry too much
about personal gains or losses,

65
00:03:56,079 --> 00:03:57,630
and don't favor either side,

66
00:03:57,630 --> 00:04:00,830
you'll be the perfect candidate
for hospital president.

67
00:04:00,870 --> 00:04:02,520
Why does this sound

68
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:04,470
more and more suspicious
the longer you talk?

69
00:04:04,470 --> 00:04:05,520
Wasn't I just a placeholder?

70
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:06,630
I'm just a temp,

71
00:04:06,630 --> 00:04:07,840
filling in until
they find someone permanent.

72
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:09,370
That was the original plan.

73
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:11,910
But leave a temporary appointment
in place long enough,

74
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:12,470
[President's Office]

75
00:04:11,910 --> 00:04:14,440
and doesn't it eventually
become permanent?

76
00:04:14,470 --> 00:04:16,480
Why won't you let Che Mingming come back?

77
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:17,190
Ask him.

78
00:04:17,190 --> 00:04:18,870
It was all his idea.

79
00:04:20,190 --> 00:04:22,450
Why won't you let Che Mingming come back?

80
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:24,080
She wants to pursue a PhD.

81
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:26,310
She's met

82
00:04:26,310 --> 00:04:27,570
all the requirements,

83
00:04:28,830 --> 00:04:30,070
but she's just a little short

84
00:04:30,070 --> 00:04:31,600
of excelling in every area.

85
00:04:31,830 --> 00:04:33,430
So I decided to cut off
her fallback option

86
00:04:33,430 --> 00:04:34,630
and push her
to give it everything she's got.

87
00:04:34,630 --> 00:04:35,830
Nothing left to lose.

88
00:04:37,430 --> 00:04:39,040
If she still doesn't get in,

89
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:42,190
President Huang will take her back.

90
00:04:42,870 --> 00:04:44,330
Anything wrong with that?

91
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:46,760
Nothing wrong with that.

92
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:49,100
Anything else, Chief Physician Liu?

93
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:57,480
Liu really

94
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:58,950
is quite a character.

95
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:00,870
P-People like him

96
00:05:00,870 --> 00:05:01,930
are hard to come by.

97
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:04,120
If he didn't have any character flaws,

98
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:06,380
would he still be at Xiaoximen Hospital?

99
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:08,540
It's all about finding the right fit.

100
00:05:08,950 --> 00:05:11,950
Just like you being the right fit
for hospital president.

101
00:05:11,950 --> 00:05:14,600
I... I don't want
to be hospital president.

102
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:17,420
I can't handle sitting in that chair.

103
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:21,830
[Security Department]

104
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:22,600
Mom, with cooking like yours,

105
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:25,280
[999 Cold Medicine]

106
00:05:23,190 --> 00:05:25,000
it'd be a crime not to open a restaurant!

107
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,480
This pickled cabbage filling

108
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:27,270
is out of this world.

109
00:05:27,270 --> 00:05:28,040
Seriously,

110
00:05:28,070 --> 00:05:30,240
I could eat it for the rest of my life
and never get tired of it.

111
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:32,100
I'll make a bigger batch next time

112
00:05:32,390 --> 00:05:34,240
and bring some over for you, Xue,

113
00:05:34,270 --> 00:05:35,670
and your father-in-law.

114
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:39,510
Set it aside

115
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:40,240
and let it cool a bit.

116
00:05:40,240 --> 00:05:41,100
Drink it later.

117
00:05:41,830 --> 00:05:42,480
It's fine.

118
00:05:43,510 --> 00:05:44,510
Put something on.

119
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:45,630
Don't get ahead of yourself.

120
00:05:45,630 --> 00:05:46,190
Have one.

121
00:05:46,190 --> 00:05:46,920
Look at that runny nose!

122
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:47,920
Come on, just eat.

123
00:05:49,270 --> 00:05:50,830
You should head home and get some sleep.

124
00:05:50,830 --> 00:05:51,630
No rush.

125
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:52,600
It's getting late.

126
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:53,600
I've got some good news

127
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:54,680
to share with you.

128
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:58,480
Good news?

129
00:05:59,630 --> 00:06:02,630
You know how I've spent
year after year fighting for justice,

130
00:06:02,630 --> 00:06:04,720
only to be talked out of it every time?

131
00:06:05,190 --> 00:06:07,590
Well, they thought
it was too much trouble,

132
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:10,600
so they asked someone
to help negotiate a settlement

133
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:11,730
and clear things up.

134
00:06:14,270 --> 00:06:15,190
I agreed.

135
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:18,260
I'm not going
to keep pushing the issue anymore.

136
00:06:18,510 --> 00:06:19,920
Back when Director Li

137
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:21,480
offered you all that money,
you turned him down

138
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:23,140
and fought him tooth and nail.

139
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,120
And now you've suddenly
had a change of heart?

140
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:27,360
That was just him trying to buy me off.

141
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:30,040
This time, they're willing to talk things
through and clear everything up.

142
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:31,190
I don't trust him.

143
00:06:31,430 --> 00:06:32,760
I trust the government.

144
00:06:34,190 --> 00:06:36,000
As long as you can find peace with it,
that's all that matters.

145
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,330
Money isn't important.

146
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:39,640
We've been saving for years,

147
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:40,750
and we've got

148
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:42,920
50,000 yuan now.

149
00:06:43,510 --> 00:06:46,310
That should be enough
for your bride price, right?

150
00:06:48,310 --> 00:06:49,560
Uncle Gong said
he doesn't want a bride price.

151
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:51,070
He may not demand one,

152
00:06:51,510 --> 00:06:53,040
but we should still give it.

153
00:06:54,159 --> 00:06:55,920
If your father-in-law won't accept it,

154
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:57,560
save it for Xue.

155
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:59,600
Let her decide what to do with it.

156
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:06,190
Mom,

157
00:07:06,190 --> 00:07:08,560
is this why you finally agreed
to stop fighting for justice?

158
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:10,040
No.

159
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,270
I'm getting old.

160
00:07:14,390 --> 00:07:16,450
I can't run around fighting anymore.

161
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:18,160
In another couple of years,

162
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:19,560
am I supposed to go around

163
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:21,560
in a wheelchair demanding justice?

164
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:23,600
I've done enough.

165
00:07:24,870 --> 00:07:26,000
It's time to stop.

166
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:26,920
Mom,

167
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:28,600
don't talk like that.

168
00:07:29,070 --> 00:07:31,600
What happened to me
has nothing to do with you.

169
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:34,480
Your quilt is way too thin.

170
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:35,390
That won't do.

171
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:37,159
I'll ask

172
00:07:37,270 --> 00:07:38,159
Nie to make you

173
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:40,560
a thicker one.

174
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:42,600
I'm heading home.

175
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:45,940
[Security Department]

176
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:05,440
Chief Physician Liu! Chief Physician Liu!

177
00:08:05,830 --> 00:08:06,680
Chief Physician Liu!

178
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:07,950
We've got a burn victim

179
00:08:07,950 --> 00:08:09,210
in the emergency room.

180
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:10,830
An electrical appliance caught fire

181
00:08:10,830 --> 00:08:12,480
and set the whole house ablaze.

182
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:13,830
He's suffered burns over 20% of his body.

183
00:08:13,830 --> 00:08:15,040
All the doctors in the burn unit

184
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,100
have been laid off,

185
00:08:16,130 --> 00:08:17,020
[Dirty Utility Room]

186
00:08:16,190 --> 00:08:17,270
and the general surgeon on duty

187
00:08:17,270 --> 00:08:18,000
has never

188
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,400
handled a case like this.

189
00:08:33,510 --> 00:08:34,150
Jia Xin.

190
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:35,510
Blood pressure: 90 over 50.

191
00:08:35,510 --> 00:08:36,909
Oxygen saturation: 98%.

192
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:38,320
Heart rate: 131.

193
00:08:38,549 --> 00:08:39,870
Infuse 500 milliliters

194
00:08:39,870 --> 00:08:40,600
of lactated Ringer's solution

195
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:41,530
intravenously.

196
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:43,240
Get blood samples ready for testing.

197
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:44,870
Insert a urinary catheter
and monitor urine output.

198
00:08:44,870 --> 00:08:46,530
Get me some povidone-iodine.

199
00:08:53,550 --> 00:08:54,840
Jia Xin, bear with me.

200
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:57,750
I'll disinfect the burn wounds
with povidone-iodine first.

201
00:08:57,750 --> 00:08:59,080
Prepare to treat the blisters.

202
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:02,320
I'll puncture the blisters at their lowest
point and drain them with a syringe.

203
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:03,440
Don't move.

204
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:04,270
Hold still.

205
00:09:04,550 --> 00:09:06,000
Here, hold his hand down for me.

206
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,330
Don't move. Don't move.

207
00:09:07,790 --> 00:09:08,920
Jia Xin, stay still.

208
00:09:10,670 --> 00:09:12,670
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts!

209
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,930
Change gloves. Drape the area.

210
00:09:17,510 --> 00:09:19,710
Get me some silver sulfadiazine cream.

211
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,000
I'm dying!

212
00:09:26,030 --> 00:09:26,960
I'm dying!

213
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:27,480
Jia Xin.

214
00:09:28,030 --> 00:09:29,230
Think about your mom.

215
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:42,670
Chief Physician Liu,

216
00:09:42,670 --> 00:09:44,150
his blood pressure is now 120 over 80.

217
00:09:44,150 --> 00:09:45,390
Oxygen saturation is 98%.

218
00:09:45,390 --> 00:09:46,320
Heart rate is 85.

219
00:09:55,790 --> 00:09:56,670
Chief Physician Liu,

220
00:09:56,670 --> 00:09:58,120
this is the patient's mother.

221
00:09:57,420 --> 00:10:01,110
[Emergency Department Lobby Ahead]

222
00:09:58,630 --> 00:09:59,960
I know. I know her.

223
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:00,750
You go take care of your other duties.

224
00:10:00,750 --> 00:10:01,390
Okay.

225
00:10:01,170 --> 00:10:05,140
[No Entry]

226
00:10:01,550 --> 00:10:02,360
Auntie Duan,

227
00:10:02,750 --> 00:10:03,550
don't worry.

228
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:04,390
Jia Xin's condition

229
00:10:04,390 --> 00:10:05,440
is stable now.

230
00:10:06,870 --> 00:10:07,840
Dr. Liu,

231
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:11,000
just seeing you puts my mind at ease.

232
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:16,030
There's 38,000 yuan on this card.

233
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:18,270
I'm old,

234
00:10:18,510 --> 00:10:20,840
and sometimes
I'm awfully slow to catch on.

235
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:21,720
I don't always

236
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:23,520
understand what people tell me,

237
00:10:24,150 --> 00:10:26,750
and I'm afraid that could
delay his treatment.

238
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:28,240
I trust you, so I'd like you

239
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:29,570
to hold on to this money.

240
00:10:30,390 --> 00:10:31,960
Please use the best medicine

241
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:34,290
and do whatever it takes
to get my son well.

242
00:10:35,630 --> 00:10:36,600
Well, I...

243
00:10:37,630 --> 00:10:39,120
Please help me out.

244
00:10:42,910 --> 00:10:44,110
All right, all right.

245
00:10:45,270 --> 00:10:46,720
Here's what we'll do, Auntie Duan.

246
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:48,080
Just write down the card's PIN for me.

247
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:49,600
I'll keep all the receipts
for every expense

248
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,840
and give them to you afterward.

249
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:51,720
Thank you.

250
00:10:51,750 --> 00:10:52,630
Thank you.

251
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:01,480
Doctor,

252
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:02,390
how is he doing?

253
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:04,840
His condition
is relatively stable for now,

254
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:06,900
but treatment will be a long process,

255
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,130
and dressing changes
will be extremely painful for him.

256
00:11:11,630 --> 00:11:13,030
I know my son.

257
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:16,870
He's always been an optimist,
ever since he was little.

258
00:11:16,870 --> 00:11:18,120
He'll get through this.

259
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:18,910
On top

260
00:11:18,910 --> 00:11:20,510
of the unbearable physical pain,

261
00:11:20,510 --> 00:11:22,320
he'll also have to cope with

262
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:23,960
the psychological trauma
caused by the changes to his face.

263
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:25,360
Right now, we need to pay close attention

264
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:26,630
to his emotional state

265
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:28,150
and make sure
he doesn't do anything drastic.

266
00:11:28,150 --> 00:11:30,630
We should arrange for as many people as
possible to take turns staying with him.

267
00:11:30,630 --> 00:11:32,080
We have only each other at home.

268
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:34,120
I... I can manage on my own.

269
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:43,030
Jia Xin,

270
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:46,790
Jia Xin.

271
00:11:49,390 --> 00:11:56,460
♪ It's only after something is lost
that we begin to see ♪

272
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:50,910
Hang in there, son.

273
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:52,720
Hang in there.

274
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:57,030
Okay, okay.

275
00:11:58,350 --> 00:12:04,090
♪ But some things can never be undone ♪

276
00:12:05,870 --> 00:12:07,120
It hurts so much.

277
00:12:07,090 --> 00:12:13,730
♪ When snowflakes cover
all our yesterdays ♪

278
00:12:10,870 --> 00:12:11,630
Miss,

279
00:12:12,070 --> 00:12:16,120
[Malatang Hot Pot]

280
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:14,000
you've been sitting here all night

281
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:14,960
without even eating.

282
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:16,200
Are you waiting for someone?

283
00:12:15,110 --> 00:12:20,920
♪ Perhaps it's best
we leave the words unsaid ♪

284
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:19,360
Duan and her son, perhaps?

285
00:12:20,750 --> 00:12:21,750
Yes.

286
00:12:22,390 --> 00:12:23,850
Have you seen them lately?

287
00:12:24,870 --> 00:12:26,440
I heard a while ago

288
00:12:24,910 --> 00:12:32,130
♪ We were once someone else ♪

289
00:12:26,670 --> 00:12:28,320
that Duan had decided to let it go

290
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:29,750
and stop fighting for justice.

291
00:12:29,750 --> 00:12:31,000
Easy, easy.

292
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:33,030
Maybe the two of them

293
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,550
have gone away for a change of scenery.

294
00:12:33,690 --> 00:12:39,880
♪ Then, one day,
we found our truest selves ♪

295
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:35,750
Girl,

296
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:36,900
it's cold out here.

297
00:12:36,910 --> 00:12:38,510
Come inside and warm up a bit.

298
00:12:39,240 --> 00:12:40,200
I'm fine, ma'am.

299
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,030
Please carry on
with what you were doing.

300
00:12:41,030 --> 00:12:42,030
Don't mind me.

301
00:12:42,690 --> 00:12:49,600
♪ Turns out,
you don't have to fall apart ♪

302
00:12:50,370 --> 00:12:57,960
♪ To deserve a fresh start ♪

303
00:12:56,050 --> 00:13:04,190
[Radiology Department] [Isolation Ward]
[Burn Department, 1st Floor]

304
00:13:00,550 --> 00:13:07,340
♪ Not every goodbye is meant to
erase the past ♪

305
00:13:04,710 --> 00:13:05,820
[Security Department]

306
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:15,340
[Fire Prevention Is Everyone's
Responsibility. Keep Safety in Mind.]

307
00:13:09,380 --> 00:13:16,200
♪ At least we met with open hearts ♪

308
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:16,910
Excuse me.

309
00:13:17,270 --> 00:13:18,480
Can I help you, miss?

310
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:20,890
♪ When life stretches on for so long ♪

311
00:13:18,750 --> 00:13:20,630
Do you know where Jia Xin went?

312
00:13:20,870 --> 00:13:22,080
I'm new here.

313
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:25,300
♪ Not every story needs a perfect ending ♪

314
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:23,940
I don't know anyone named Jia Xin.

315
00:13:26,020 --> 00:13:34,050
♪ Maybe walking side by side
for a while is enough ♪

316
00:13:27,150 --> 00:13:28,350
It's okay. Thank you.

317
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:30,390
Take care.

318
00:13:42,630 --> 00:13:43,270
Please look after him for me

319
00:13:43,270 --> 00:13:44,840
while you're there.

320
00:13:44,050 --> 00:13:46,000
[Civilized Fucheng]

321
00:13:45,750 --> 00:13:46,240
Don't mention it.

322
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:47,510
You can rest easy.

323
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:49,130
I've got it covered.

324
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:51,000
Sometimes, when it comes to family...

325
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,120
Do your parents know

326
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:53,360
about my dad's condition?

327
00:13:52,930 --> 00:13:56,990
[Drinking Water]

328
00:13:54,030 --> 00:13:54,840
No.

329
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:56,500
I haven't told them anything.

330
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:59,400
Don't you think that's a little unwise?

331
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,080
What are you worried about?

332
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:02,670
You don't need to worry about a thing.

333
00:14:02,670 --> 00:14:05,130
Uncle Che and I
get along like a house on fire.

334
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:08,240
Rest assured,

335
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:10,240
I'll live up
to the organization's expectations

336
00:14:10,240 --> 00:14:11,550
and bring Uncle Che back safe and sound.

337
00:14:11,550 --> 00:14:12,600
Can you stop acting up, especially

338
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:14,260
with your parents right here?

339
00:14:14,510 --> 00:14:16,030
Yes, Commissioner Che.

340
00:14:17,720 --> 00:14:18,440
What,

341
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:19,970
are we on the same level now?

342
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:23,570
Sorry, leader. I overstepped.

343
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:25,480
Cut the crap.

344
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:27,510
Go inside already. It's here.

345
00:14:27,510 --> 00:14:28,320
Dad, we're here.

346
00:14:28,320 --> 00:14:29,960
Uncle Che, here is the ticket gate.

347
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:31,240
-We're leaving, Mom and Dad.
-Keep your ID card somewhere safe.

348
00:14:31,240 --> 00:14:32,550
-Take good care of yourself, son.
-Remember what I told you.

349
00:14:32,550 --> 00:14:33,550
Call us anytime.

350
00:14:36,550 --> 00:14:37,320
Junnan,

351
00:14:37,750 --> 00:14:39,080
take good care of my dad.

352
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:40,840
And look after yourself, too.

353
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:41,630
Don't worry.

354
00:14:41,870 --> 00:14:43,120
Consider it done.

355
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:44,960
Director Chen.

356
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:46,510
Have a safe trip, Mr. Che.

357
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:47,120
All right, all right.

358
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:47,910
You two head home.

359
00:14:47,910 --> 00:14:48,360
-Take...
-Bye-bye.

360
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:49,870
Take good care of Uncle Che.

361
00:14:49,870 --> 00:14:50,960
I'll send you photos

362
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:52,080
and videos.

363
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:53,440
Do you think our son

364
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:54,960
is ready for this new chapter in his life?

365
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:55,840
Clearly not.

366
00:14:55,840 --> 00:14:57,360
-But this is a start...
-Uncle, Auntie,

367
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:58,670
um, I'd better get going.

368
00:14:58,670 --> 00:14:59,480
I'll give you a ride.

369
00:14:59,480 --> 00:14:59,840
No, no, it's fine.

370
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:01,320
The bus is really convenient for me.

371
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:02,550
Well, we're going the same way anyway.

372
00:15:02,550 --> 00:15:03,550
Um, Chen,

373
00:15:03,550 --> 00:15:04,550
weren't you in a hurry to get to work?

374
00:15:04,550 --> 00:15:04,840
Yes.

375
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:05,550
You go ahead and drive back.

376
00:15:05,550 --> 00:15:06,390
We'll take the bus.

377
00:15:06,390 --> 00:15:07,750
Don't rush off just yet.

378
00:15:07,750 --> 00:15:08,960
What if... what if

379
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:10,290
she has something to do?

380
00:15:10,550 --> 00:15:11,150
Miss,

381
00:15:11,150 --> 00:15:12,550
maybe we could meet again sometime?

382
00:15:12,550 --> 00:15:13,120
Sure.

383
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:14,980
Well, goodbye, Uncle and Auntie.

384
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:16,360
Take care!

385
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:21,720
[Radiology Department] [Isolation Ward]
[Burn Department, 1st Floor]

386
00:15:22,320 --> 00:15:24,390
-It's okay, it's okay. You're all right.
-What's wrong? Are you feeling unwell?

387
00:15:24,390 --> 00:15:25,600
He had a nightmare.

388
00:15:25,910 --> 00:15:28,570
Bed two, Jia Xin.
Time for your dressing change.

389
00:15:28,910 --> 00:15:29,550
Mom.

390
00:15:30,240 --> 00:15:31,570
No, no. Don't change it.

391
00:15:31,630 --> 00:15:32,390
Please, don't.

392
00:15:32,390 --> 00:15:33,360
The medication he was prescribed

393
00:15:33,360 --> 00:15:34,960
should have
some pain-relieving ingredients.

394
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:37,160
He's taken them, but he's still in pain.

395
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:39,390
He can't even sleep at night.

396
00:15:39,870 --> 00:15:40,870
Dr. Liu,

397
00:15:41,150 --> 00:15:42,080
could we

398
00:15:42,270 --> 00:15:44,030
wait a few more days
before changing his dressing?

399
00:15:44,030 --> 00:15:44,600
I'm afraid not, ma'am.

400
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:45,440
You need
to follow the doctor's instructions

401
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:46,150
and have the dressings changed
on schedule.

402
00:15:46,150 --> 00:15:47,510
Otherwise, what if
the wounds get infected?

403
00:15:47,510 --> 00:15:48,840
Don't be scared. Being afraid
will only make it feel worse.

404
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:50,030
No, no!

405
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:51,910
Mom, it hurts too much.

406
00:15:52,270 --> 00:15:53,360
Don't change it.

407
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:54,270
Please, just leave it alone.

408
00:15:54,270 --> 00:15:55,600
I know it hurts, my son.

409
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:57,000
Just leave it alone.

410
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:58,800
We have to push through the pain.

411
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:00,670
I'll be as gentle as I can.

412
00:16:00,670 --> 00:16:02,550
Please, doctor. I'm begging you.

413
00:16:02,870 --> 00:16:04,480
It hurts so much. Please!

414
00:16:08,150 --> 00:16:08,750
Uncle Che.

415
00:16:13,300 --> 00:16:16,530
[Chen Junnan]

416
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:19,480
You must be Mr. Wang.

417
00:16:19,510 --> 00:16:21,550
Are you Mr. Chen and Mr. Che?

418
00:16:21,550 --> 00:16:22,200
That's right.

419
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:22,870
I'm a colleague

420
00:16:22,870 --> 00:16:23,630
of Manager Liu.

421
00:16:23,630 --> 00:16:24,960
I've come to pick you up.

422
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:25,870
Manager Liu?

423
00:16:25,870 --> 00:16:27,120
Which Manager Liu?

424
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:28,450
Y-You mean Zhengguang?

425
00:16:28,670 --> 00:16:29,600
Liu Zhengguang.

426
00:16:30,630 --> 00:16:31,960
Zhengguang's a manager now?

427
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:33,490
Yes, yes. He's our manager.

428
00:16:33,630 --> 00:16:34,460
Hello. Nice to meet you.

429
00:16:34,460 --> 00:16:39,330
[Guomao Bridge]

430
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:36,870
Standing

431
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:40,460
on the banks of the Lancang River,

432
00:16:40,790 --> 00:16:42,990
I always wished I could fill a washbasin

433
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:46,030
with its surging waves.

434
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:49,360
Then one morning,

435
00:16:49,670 --> 00:16:51,440
after the waters had receded,

436
00:16:52,750 --> 00:16:55,440
I saw the rocks studded with pearls.

437
00:16:58,720 --> 00:17:00,480
They were the moons

438
00:17:01,630 --> 00:17:03,550
the river had failed to carry away

439
00:17:05,349 --> 00:17:06,349
the night before.

440
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:09,030
Uncle Che,

441
00:17:09,270 --> 00:17:10,530
what a beautiful poem!

442
00:17:13,589 --> 00:17:14,400
Junnan.

443
00:17:19,030 --> 00:17:20,510
Look at you, all dressed up
in your black suit and leather shoes.

444
00:17:20,510 --> 00:17:22,109
You've really smartened up!

445
00:17:22,349 --> 00:17:23,200
Let me introduce you.

446
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:24,200
This is Uncle Che.

447
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:25,480
Hello, Uncle Che.

448
00:17:26,109 --> 00:17:26,920
You must be the liaison

449
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:28,270
from the Beijing station.

450
00:17:28,270 --> 00:17:28,880
I know.

451
00:17:30,110 --> 00:17:30,840
Zhengguang.

452
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:31,930
Liu Zhengguang.

453
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:32,550
That's me.

454
00:17:32,550 --> 00:17:33,440
Xiaobo, right?

455
00:17:33,750 --> 00:17:34,480
Liu Zhengguang.

456
00:17:34,480 --> 00:17:35,550
Just call him Zhengguang.

457
00:17:35,550 --> 00:17:35,790
Right, right.

458
00:17:35,790 --> 00:17:36,200
Come on, have a seat.

459
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:36,960
Time to eat, Uncle Che.

460
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:38,160
Comrade Zhengguang,
you've been working hard.

461
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:38,880
-Oh, not at all. Not at all.
-You've really gone to a lot of trouble.

462
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:39,680
It's nothing.

463
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:41,740
Have a seat, Uncle Che.

464
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:43,240
You've got things

465
00:17:44,030 --> 00:17:45,880
pretty well arranged here.

466
00:17:48,350 --> 00:17:49,830
Now tell me, what's going on?

467
00:17:49,830 --> 00:17:50,680
A little luck,

468
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:52,810
and a little help from Liu Zhengliang.

469
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:00,400
What brings you here?

470
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:01,790
Boss,

471
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:04,000
everyone back at the station
sends their regards.

472
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,660
I came to see how you're doing.

473
00:18:06,510 --> 00:18:07,480
Leave the stuff

474
00:18:07,550 --> 00:18:08,350
and go.

475
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:09,960
All right.

476
00:18:10,110 --> 00:18:10,790
You didn't

477
00:18:10,790 --> 00:18:12,050
have to bring all this.

478
00:18:13,110 --> 00:18:14,370
I'll be off then, Boss.

479
00:18:15,510 --> 00:18:16,230
Wait.

480
00:18:18,310 --> 00:18:19,720
Don't think saving my life

481
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:21,270
gives you any special privileges.

482
00:18:21,270 --> 00:18:23,200
I'm not going to treat you
any differently because of it.

483
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:24,930
That's fine. Whatever you say.

484
00:18:24,960 --> 00:18:26,350
As long as you stay healthy

485
00:18:26,350 --> 00:18:27,160
and don't end up back in the hospital,

486
00:18:27,160 --> 00:18:28,560
that's all that matters.

487
00:18:29,550 --> 00:18:30,410
Go on, get back.

488
00:18:32,590 --> 00:18:33,990
Take care on your way out.

489
00:18:46,070 --> 00:18:47,000
Liu Zhengguang!

490
00:18:47,590 --> 00:18:48,790
Liu Zhengguang!

491
00:18:50,750 --> 00:18:51,550
Who is it?

492
00:18:52,510 --> 00:18:54,270
The man who's offering you a job.

493
00:18:54,270 --> 00:18:55,550
I don't even know you.

494
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:57,050
Get in the car first.

495
00:18:57,350 --> 00:18:59,480
We'll get acquainted after you get in.

496
00:19:01,110 --> 00:19:02,440
I've known Wu

497
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:03,830
for years,

498
00:19:04,110 --> 00:19:06,200
and this is the first time
he's ever asked me for a favor.

499
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:08,270
He called me out of the blue

500
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:10,170
and put in a strong word for you.

501
00:19:11,110 --> 00:19:12,750
As it happens, my driver

502
00:19:12,750 --> 00:19:14,950
just quit and went back to his hometown.

503
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:17,920
How about staying on
and working as my driver?

504
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:19,320
Would you be interested?

505
00:19:23,640 --> 00:19:24,480
Later, I found out

506
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:26,070
my current boss's surname was Zheng.

507
00:19:26,070 --> 00:19:28,870
He and Boss Wu had served
in the military together.

508
00:19:29,830 --> 00:19:31,200
But everyone

509
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:32,260
calls you Manager.

510
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:34,920
Well, besides driving for the boss,

511
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:36,270
I'm also learning the ropes
in the hotel's

512
00:19:36,270 --> 00:19:37,330
sales department.

513
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:39,240
We've got

514
00:19:39,350 --> 00:19:40,310
one sales manager

515
00:19:40,310 --> 00:19:41,680
and seven deputy managers
in the sales department.

516
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:42,550
They're all managers anyway,

517
00:19:42,550 --> 00:19:43,270
so we basically

518
00:19:43,270 --> 00:19:44,600
call everyone Manager.

519
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:47,200
I hope

520
00:19:48,920 --> 00:19:49,880
every kind-hearted person

521
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:51,200
gets as lucky as you.

522
00:20:35,350 --> 00:20:36,550
Chief Physician Liu.

523
00:20:39,440 --> 00:20:41,730
[Wishing You a Speedy Recovery]

524
00:20:41,730 --> 00:20:44,300
[Beware of medical scammers.
Don't be fooled.]

525
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:57,400
[Ward 1]

526
00:21:01,310 --> 00:21:04,690
[No Smoking Area]

527
00:21:05,050 --> 00:21:06,430
[Quiet]

528
00:21:13,850 --> 00:21:14,660
[Restroom]

529
00:21:14,760 --> 00:21:15,360
[Friendly Reminder]

530
00:21:15,380 --> 00:21:16,770
[Please do not dispose of toilet paper
or sanitary products]

531
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:19,580
[in the squat toilet,
as this may cause blockages.]

532
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:20,260
[Squat Toilet]

533
00:21:20,590 --> 00:21:21,510
[Seated Toilet]

534
00:21:21,510 --> 00:21:21,840
[Squat Toilet]

535
00:21:21,930 --> 00:21:22,460
[Seated Toilet]

536
00:21:26,240 --> 00:21:27,030
Jia Xin.

537
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:30,720
Jia Xin.

538
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:32,270
Are you in there?

539
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:35,510
Jia Xin.

540
00:21:35,790 --> 00:21:36,590
Jia Xin!

541
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:42,510
Zhengliang.

542
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:44,900
Don't come any closer.

543
00:21:45,270 --> 00:21:46,270
Give me the knife.

544
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:49,480
L-Listen to me.

545
00:21:50,960 --> 00:21:52,160
Your life is your own.

546
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:53,920
Whether you

547
00:21:54,160 --> 00:21:55,350
live or die,

548
00:21:55,350 --> 00:21:56,310
it's up to you.

549
00:21:57,160 --> 00:21:58,890
But even if you're going to die,

550
00:21:59,070 --> 00:21:59,960
shouldn't we at least

551
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:01,160
talk through

552
00:22:01,160 --> 00:22:01,960
whatever's weighing on your mind first?

553
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:03,350
It hurts so much.

554
00:22:04,480 --> 00:22:05,920
I can't take it anymore.

555
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:06,310
I know.

556
00:22:06,310 --> 00:22:07,510
I know you're in pain.

557
00:22:07,590 --> 00:22:08,200
But give me the knife first.

558
00:22:08,200 --> 00:22:10,070
I'm going to be crippled
for the rest of my life.

559
00:22:10,070 --> 00:22:11,510
I'll never get better.

560
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:13,680
You're not me.

561
00:22:14,240 --> 00:22:15,880
You don't know what it's like.

562
00:22:15,880 --> 00:22:17,160
My face is ruined.

563
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:19,550
I'll never recover.

564
00:22:19,830 --> 00:22:20,680
I'm ruined!

565
00:22:20,680 --> 00:22:22,640
You're not ruined! It can be treated.

566
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:24,030
It can all be treated.

567
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:25,270
Trust me.

568
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:26,960
Everyone

569
00:22:27,480 --> 00:22:29,740
is doing everything they can to help you.

570
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:30,830
But you have to

571
00:22:30,830 --> 00:22:32,470
keep fighting, okay?

572
00:22:33,590 --> 00:22:36,480
-Give me the knife.
-How am I supposed to hang in there?

573
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:39,280
My mom can't even afford
to get her stones treated.

574
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:42,720
I'm nothing but a burden to her now.

575
00:22:42,720 --> 00:22:43,440
No.

576
00:22:43,440 --> 00:22:44,680
Your mom told me

577
00:22:45,070 --> 00:22:47,070
you were always so optimistic growing up.

578
00:22:47,070 --> 00:22:50,160
-She believes in you, and so do I.
-What good is being optimistic?

579
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:50,960
Can it make me

580
00:22:50,960 --> 00:22:52,510
look the way I used to

581
00:22:52,920 --> 00:22:54,780
and let me live with some dignity?

582
00:22:56,030 --> 00:22:57,680
My mom has sacrificed

583
00:22:57,680 --> 00:22:59,160
her whole life for me.

584
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,070
I'm nothing but a useless wreck now.

585
00:23:02,270 --> 00:23:03,070
Jia Xin.

586
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,270
If you die, it'll all be over for you.

587
00:23:07,270 --> 00:23:08,600
But what about your mom?

588
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:10,270
She's getting on in years.

589
00:23:10,270 --> 00:23:12,070
Do you really want to leave her all alone?

590
00:23:12,070 --> 00:23:13,750
I want to live, too.

591
00:23:14,350 --> 00:23:15,720
But how?

592
00:23:16,070 --> 00:23:18,000
How am I supposed to live like this?

593
00:23:24,960 --> 00:23:26,560
The other day, on my way home,

594
00:23:28,440 --> 00:23:29,840
I was sitting in a vehicle

595
00:23:31,550 --> 00:23:34,150
when I saw a makeshift shelter
by the roadside.

596
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:39,500
You and your mom were sitting inside.

597
00:23:49,920 --> 00:23:50,720
Jia Xin,

598
00:23:52,680 --> 00:23:53,960
I really envy you.

599
00:23:58,030 --> 00:23:58,590
I do.

600
00:24:28,680 --> 00:24:29,510
It's okay.

601
00:24:31,440 --> 00:24:32,640
It can all be treated.

602
00:24:33,880 --> 00:24:36,210
Things will get better, little by little.

603
00:24:38,350 --> 00:24:39,160
Zhengliang.

604
00:24:42,110 --> 00:24:44,110
Can you please not tell my mom?

605
00:24:47,640 --> 00:24:49,400
I don't want her to worry.

606
00:25:07,720 --> 00:25:08,920
What's wrong?

607
00:25:09,830 --> 00:25:11,000
Are you in a bad mood?

608
00:25:12,790 --> 00:25:14,680
I have a patient with severe burns.

609
00:25:14,680 --> 00:25:16,410
He's a friend of Zhengguang's.

610
00:25:16,830 --> 00:25:17,750
He tried to kill himself,

611
00:25:17,750 --> 00:25:19,150
but I managed to save him.

612
00:25:19,400 --> 00:25:21,460
I'm still worried he might try again.

613
00:25:43,110 --> 00:25:43,880
Kid,

614
00:25:44,590 --> 00:25:46,640
I heard you're bored.

615
00:25:47,110 --> 00:25:49,110
So, uh, Xiaozhu

616
00:25:49,110 --> 00:25:50,350
brought all kinds of games:

617
00:25:50,350 --> 00:25:51,590
Chinese military chess,
Chinese chess, checkers,

618
00:25:51,590 --> 00:25:52,590
and Gomoku.

619
00:25:52,590 --> 00:25:54,200
Whatever you feel like playing,
we'll play.

620
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:55,030
And if you're still bored,

621
00:25:55,030 --> 00:25:56,200
we can just sit and chat.

622
00:25:56,200 --> 00:25:56,640
How's that?

623
00:25:56,640 --> 00:25:57,720
Forget chatting.

624
00:25:57,720 --> 00:25:58,550
If you want a drink,

625
00:25:58,550 --> 00:25:59,720
I'll even,

626
00:25:59,720 --> 00:26:00,240
you know...

627
00:26:00,240 --> 00:26:02,300
He'll even have a few drinks with you.

628
00:26:02,680 --> 00:26:03,750
I can't have you guys

629
00:26:03,750 --> 00:26:05,440
keeping his company for nothing.

630
00:26:05,440 --> 00:26:07,590
I ought to show my appreciation somehow.

631
00:26:07,590 --> 00:26:08,550
Come on, don't say that.

632
00:26:08,550 --> 00:26:09,720
You're making it awkward.

633
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:11,640
Bring some sunflower seeds, then.

634
00:26:11,640 --> 00:26:12,440
Sure.

635
00:26:15,270 --> 00:26:16,680
Everyone,

636
00:26:19,640 --> 00:26:20,970
why don't you head home?

637
00:26:22,070 --> 00:26:23,030
Look at him,

638
00:26:23,030 --> 00:26:24,200
being all polite.

639
00:26:24,200 --> 00:26:24,920
No,

640
00:26:25,350 --> 00:26:26,550
I'm not being polite.

641
00:26:27,440 --> 00:26:29,200
Mom, I want to see Zhengliang.

642
00:26:29,200 --> 00:26:29,790
Here.

643
00:26:29,790 --> 00:26:30,650
I'm right here.

644
00:26:31,550 --> 00:26:32,350
What's up?

645
00:26:32,680 --> 00:26:33,960
Are you itchy or in pain?

646
00:26:33,960 --> 00:26:34,790
Neither.

647
00:26:35,960 --> 00:26:37,420
I just wanted to thank you.

648
00:26:38,200 --> 00:26:39,260
Forget the thanks.

649
00:26:39,680 --> 00:26:40,550
Let me ask you something.

650
00:26:40,550 --> 00:26:42,350
If Liu Zhengguang and I
ever get into an argument,

651
00:26:42,350 --> 00:26:43,310
whose side will you take?

652
00:26:43,310 --> 00:26:46,440
I'll take the side of whoever's right,
of course.

653
00:26:49,200 --> 00:26:50,460
Can't argue with that.

654
00:26:52,640 --> 00:26:54,100
You're a pretty smart guy.

655
00:26:54,350 --> 00:26:55,160
Zhengliang,

656
00:26:56,350 --> 00:26:58,160
I need to ask you for a favor.

657
00:27:00,220 --> 00:27:01,970
[Construction Area. Do Not Climb Over.]

658
00:27:02,050 --> 00:27:03,430
[Gong's Blind Massage]

659
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:12,680
Hello.

660
00:27:12,920 --> 00:27:13,590
Hello.

661
00:27:13,590 --> 00:27:15,110
What kind of service are you looking for?

662
00:27:15,110 --> 00:27:15,920
I'm not here for any of your services.

663
00:27:15,920 --> 00:27:16,510
I'm a doctor

664
00:27:16,510 --> 00:27:17,830
at Xiaoximen Hospital.

665
00:27:17,830 --> 00:27:19,230
I'm looking for Gong Xue.

666
00:27:20,270 --> 00:27:22,130
Sweetie, someone's here for you.

667
00:27:30,310 --> 00:27:31,000
Um,

668
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:31,790
Jia Xin told me

669
00:27:31,790 --> 00:27:33,070
he owed you 3,000 yuan,

670
00:27:33,160 --> 00:27:35,090
and asked me to pay you back for him.

671
00:27:35,550 --> 00:27:36,640
Here's

672
00:27:37,310 --> 00:27:38,720
the 3,000 yuan in cash.

673
00:27:38,960 --> 00:27:40,160
Go ahead and count it.

674
00:27:41,880 --> 00:27:43,240
What's this all about?

675
00:27:44,550 --> 00:27:45,750
He just told me he owed you money

676
00:27:45,750 --> 00:27:46,880
and asked me to pay it back.

677
00:27:46,880 --> 00:27:48,480
He didn't say anything else.

678
00:27:50,270 --> 00:27:50,880
How could he

679
00:27:50,880 --> 00:27:52,510
not even want to see me?

680
00:27:54,240 --> 00:27:56,170
Sweetie, don't get upset just yet.

681
00:27:57,240 --> 00:27:58,100
How about this?

682
00:27:58,160 --> 00:27:59,200
Where is he?

683
00:27:59,200 --> 00:28:00,750
Take me to see him.

684
00:28:00,750 --> 00:28:01,790
Whatever's going on, I'll—

685
00:28:01,790 --> 00:28:02,440
Dad.

686
00:28:08,880 --> 00:28:09,750
Sir,

687
00:28:10,720 --> 00:28:12,380
please go back and tell Jia Xin

688
00:28:13,350 --> 00:28:15,640
that even if he doesn't want
to see me anymore,

689
00:28:15,640 --> 00:28:17,370
he should tell me that himself.

690
00:28:17,510 --> 00:28:19,550
He can't just disappear like this.

691
00:28:21,160 --> 00:28:21,830
All right.

692
00:28:21,830 --> 00:28:23,760
I'll make sure he gets the message.

693
00:28:25,880 --> 00:28:26,270
Well,

694
00:28:26,270 --> 00:28:27,790
if the amount is correct,

695
00:28:27,830 --> 00:28:28,760
I'll be on my way.

696
00:28:39,070 --> 00:28:39,720
Sweetie, please,

697
00:28:39,720 --> 00:28:41,310
d-don't be mad.

698
00:28:43,640 --> 00:28:44,680
This is my fault.

699
00:28:45,960 --> 00:28:47,110
I misjudged him.

700
00:28:52,720 --> 00:28:53,480
Um,

701
00:28:52,760 --> 00:29:02,680
[Lounge]

702
00:28:53,920 --> 00:28:54,720
I'm sorry,

703
00:28:54,880 --> 00:28:55,750
Sir and Miss.

704
00:28:55,920 --> 00:28:57,980
I wasn't thinking straight just now.

705
00:28:58,240 --> 00:29:00,110
Do you know what condition

706
00:29:00,720 --> 00:29:01,720
Jia Xin is in now?

707
00:29:03,960 --> 00:29:04,750
Jia Xin.

708
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:07,920
Jia Xin, what's with you paying me back?

709
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:09,350
What do you take me for?

710
00:29:14,790 --> 00:29:16,160
I... I'm disfigured.

711
00:29:33,920 --> 00:29:34,720
Don't...

712
00:29:55,960 --> 00:29:57,760
What does that have to do with me?

713
00:29:58,480 --> 00:29:59,110
It's not like I can see

714
00:29:59,110 --> 00:30:00,510
what you look like.

715
00:30:00,640 --> 00:30:01,350
What,

716
00:30:01,350 --> 00:30:03,480
were you really that handsome before?

717
00:30:08,510 --> 00:30:09,310
Pretty much.

718
00:30:10,160 --> 00:30:11,640
Before I lost my sight,

719
00:30:12,200 --> 00:30:13,600
Andy Lau was my favorite.

720
00:30:14,270 --> 00:30:15,730
Are you as handsome as him?

721
00:30:16,030 --> 00:30:17,430
I'd say we're about even.

722
00:30:17,960 --> 00:30:18,830
Liar.

723
00:30:19,830 --> 00:30:21,070
You feel like a steamed bun,

724
00:30:21,070 --> 00:30:24,070
and you're telling me you were
as handsome as Andy Lau?

725
00:30:26,310 --> 00:30:28,070
At least it feels nice to touch.

726
00:30:46,110 --> 00:30:46,920
Jia Xin.

727
00:30:47,350 --> 00:30:48,160
Here.

728
00:30:49,830 --> 00:30:50,720
When you

729
00:30:51,720 --> 00:30:52,830
get better,

730
00:30:53,640 --> 00:30:54,400
will you still

731
00:30:54,400 --> 00:30:55,680
read novels to me?

732
00:30:56,550 --> 00:30:58,410
You don't have to wait until then.

733
00:30:58,680 --> 00:31:00,140
I can read to you right now.

734
00:31:03,070 --> 00:31:06,920
Last time, we left off

735
00:31:08,750 --> 00:31:11,160
with Li Mochou and her disciple

736
00:31:12,160 --> 00:31:15,160
turning this little town upside down,

737
00:31:15,160 --> 00:31:19,110
throwing everything into chaos.

738
00:31:24,070 --> 00:31:27,640
Meanwhile, Yang Guo was lying peacefully

739
00:31:27,750 --> 00:31:29,070
on the same heated bed

740
00:31:29,070 --> 00:31:31,680
as Lu Wushuang.

741
00:31:35,200 --> 00:31:37,960
Lu Wushuang wondered to herself,

742
00:31:38,640 --> 00:31:40,270
"Is Yang Guo

743
00:31:40,550 --> 00:31:44,240
a fool or a sly fox?

744
00:31:45,070 --> 00:31:46,590
If he's a fool,

745
00:31:48,880 --> 00:31:51,640
how can he be so clever?"

746
00:31:59,310 --> 00:32:01,590
From then on, I began to understand

747
00:32:02,200 --> 00:32:04,590
that everyone has two lives.

748
00:32:05,400 --> 00:32:06,510
Your second life begins

749
00:32:06,510 --> 00:32:08,440
when you realize

750
00:32:09,400 --> 00:32:10,960
you only

751
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:12,400
have one life.

752
00:32:17,400 --> 00:32:18,920
Do you know

753
00:32:19,270 --> 00:32:21,470
why I sent you away when you were little?

754
00:32:23,750 --> 00:32:24,920
Because I was sick.

755
00:32:27,750 --> 00:32:28,550
No.

756
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:31,110
I was scared.

757
00:32:32,110 --> 00:32:33,510
I was afraid you'd suffer

758
00:32:34,110 --> 00:32:35,170
if you stayed here.

759
00:32:42,920 --> 00:32:44,240
Sometimes, fear

760
00:32:45,070 --> 00:32:46,510
comes from caring.

761
00:32:48,480 --> 00:32:49,270
Son,

762
00:32:49,920 --> 00:32:51,650
stop being so hard on yourself.

763
00:32:52,350 --> 00:32:53,550
You and that girl...

764
00:32:54,110 --> 00:32:55,270
Deep down,

765
00:32:55,590 --> 00:32:57,790
you already know the answer, don't you?

766
00:33:15,830 --> 00:33:17,370
When I went looking for you today,

767
00:33:17,370 --> 00:33:22,460
[Electrical Panel. Danger: High Voltage.]
[No Smoking. No Open Flames.]

768
00:33:18,160 --> 00:33:20,560
they told me you were
in the operating room.

769
00:33:20,750 --> 00:33:22,350
I figured you hadn't eaten,

770
00:33:23,110 --> 00:33:23,880
right?

771
00:33:26,590 --> 00:33:27,790
How is it?

772
00:33:29,270 --> 00:33:30,070
It's okay.

773
00:33:31,880 --> 00:33:32,550
Oh, come on.

774
00:33:32,550 --> 00:33:33,510
"It's okay"?

775
00:33:33,510 --> 00:33:35,110
Can't you just say it's good?

776
00:33:37,590 --> 00:33:38,400
It's good.

777
00:33:42,160 --> 00:33:44,360
Why are you being so cooperative today?

778
00:33:49,070 --> 00:33:49,720
Ai Chen,

779
00:33:49,720 --> 00:33:52,180
how about we keep things this way
from now on?

780
00:33:52,680 --> 00:33:53,920
In your dreams!

781
00:33:54,440 --> 00:33:56,770
You think I'm gonna cook
for you every day?

782
00:33:57,270 --> 00:33:58,270
I let you get a little comfortable,

783
00:33:58,270 --> 00:33:59,720
and now you're getting carried away?

784
00:33:59,720 --> 00:34:00,720
Not happening!

785
00:34:01,270 --> 00:34:02,590
That's not what I meant.

786
00:34:02,590 --> 00:34:03,850
Then what did you mean?

787
00:34:07,350 --> 00:34:08,150
Nothing.

788
00:34:15,420 --> 00:34:15,880
[Electrical Panel. Danger: High Voltage.]

789
00:34:19,710 --> 00:34:20,639
Come on, tell me.

790
00:34:21,800 --> 00:34:24,400
Are you thinking
what I think you're thinking?

791
00:34:25,400 --> 00:34:26,280
What?

792
00:34:28,510 --> 00:34:29,590
Is it?

793
00:34:30,030 --> 00:34:31,030
Hurry up,

794
00:34:31,960 --> 00:34:33,030
tell me.

795
00:34:34,480 --> 00:34:35,590
Is it or not?

796
00:34:36,150 --> 00:34:37,880
Where's this call coming from?

797
00:34:38,800 --> 00:34:40,190
Why isn't this quite

798
00:34:40,190 --> 00:34:41,320
what I imagined?

799
00:34:42,710 --> 00:34:43,510
Answer it.

800
00:34:43,510 --> 00:34:44,590
Sounds urgent.

801
00:34:45,480 --> 00:34:46,280
Just a second.

802
00:34:46,800 --> 00:34:47,590
Hello.

803
00:34:49,800 --> 00:34:51,000
Mr. Tan, right?

804
00:34:51,510 --> 00:34:53,110
I heard from your mother

805
00:34:53,110 --> 00:34:54,370
that you're overseas.

806
00:34:56,280 --> 00:34:56,920
Yes.

807
00:34:56,920 --> 00:34:59,440
We were going over the list

808
00:34:59,440 --> 00:35:00,970
until after 4 AM yesterday.

809
00:35:02,920 --> 00:35:04,550
The songs are set:
"Eighteen Levels of Hell,"

810
00:35:04,550 --> 00:35:05,670
"Seven Gates of Mourning,"

811
00:35:05,670 --> 00:35:06,480
and...

812
00:35:08,360 --> 00:35:10,160
Oh, we can sing "Grand Funeral."

813
00:35:11,400 --> 00:35:12,360
I... I can't do it right now.

814
00:35:12,360 --> 00:35:12,960
I'm out at the moment.

815
00:35:12,960 --> 00:35:15,220
How about I sing it
for you a little later?

816
00:35:16,000 --> 00:35:18,260
You're waiting for a connecting flight?

817
00:35:18,320 --> 00:35:19,760
-But on my end...
-It's fine.

818
00:35:19,760 --> 00:35:21,160
This room is soundproof.

819
00:35:21,840 --> 00:35:23,320
Mr. Tan, I'm all set here.

820
00:35:24,360 --> 00:35:25,150
And...

821
00:35:25,480 --> 00:35:26,960
please accept my condolences.

822
00:35:26,960 --> 00:35:27,960
"Grand Funeral."

823
00:35:28,800 --> 00:35:36,280
Love and hate linger on,

824
00:35:37,000 --> 00:35:43,400
through generations of joy and sorrow.

825
00:35:45,280 --> 00:35:51,590
The long road of life

826
00:35:52,840 --> 00:35:59,110
is filled with one trial after another...

827
00:36:03,590 --> 00:36:05,190
Mr. Tan, are you still there?

828
00:36:07,840 --> 00:36:08,550
I understand, I really do.

829
00:36:08,550 --> 00:36:10,810
I really understand how you're feeling.

830
00:36:10,880 --> 00:36:12,230
Then it's settled.

831
00:36:13,230 --> 00:36:14,320
All right, all right. Don't worry.

832
00:36:14,320 --> 00:36:15,110
I'll have everything

833
00:36:15,110 --> 00:36:16,770
taken care of before you land.

834
00:36:17,480 --> 00:36:18,680
All right, all right.

835
00:36:20,400 --> 00:36:21,070
Well...

836
00:36:22,280 --> 00:36:23,280
Just imagine how awful he must feel

837
00:36:23,280 --> 00:36:24,960
up there on the plane.

838
00:36:33,510 --> 00:36:34,440
What were you...

839
00:36:35,400 --> 00:36:36,670
what were you about to say just now?

840
00:36:36,670 --> 00:36:37,920
Say it again.

841
00:36:39,190 --> 00:36:40,070
I forgot.

842
00:36:40,630 --> 00:36:41,840
How could you forget?

843
00:36:43,590 --> 00:36:45,510
It's just the two of us here.

844
00:36:45,510 --> 00:36:47,070
What's there to be embarrassed about?

845
00:36:47,070 --> 00:36:47,960
I'm not embarrassed.

846
00:36:47,960 --> 00:36:49,090
I really did forget.

847
00:36:49,670 --> 00:36:51,510
We're both Northeasterners
through and through.

848
00:36:51,510 --> 00:36:53,070
Don't be so hesitant.

849
00:36:55,510 --> 00:36:56,970
You know what? Never mind.

850
00:36:57,150 --> 00:36:58,280
Don't say anything.

851
00:37:01,670 --> 00:37:02,480
I'll say it.

852
00:37:05,510 --> 00:37:07,030
When it comes to someone I like,

853
00:37:07,030 --> 00:37:09,290
I have no problem putting my pride aside.

854
00:37:10,070 --> 00:37:11,030
From now on,

855
00:37:12,070 --> 00:37:13,360
if you haven't eaten

856
00:37:13,360 --> 00:37:14,670
and I'm free, I'll cook for you

857
00:37:14,670 --> 00:37:15,510
and bring you a nice,

858
00:37:15,510 --> 00:37:16,400
hot meal.

859
00:37:16,550 --> 00:37:17,190
But there's one thing

860
00:37:17,190 --> 00:37:18,920
we need to agree on first.

861
00:37:19,320 --> 00:37:20,550
If I can't bring you food,

862
00:37:20,550 --> 00:37:21,950
you can't just go hungry.

863
00:37:22,360 --> 00:37:23,490
Eating irregularly

864
00:37:23,880 --> 00:37:24,960
like that

865
00:37:24,960 --> 00:37:26,160
can't be good for you.

866
00:37:26,800 --> 00:37:27,630
I'm

867
00:37:28,800 --> 00:37:29,760
pretty good

868
00:37:29,760 --> 00:37:30,840
at taking care of myself,

869
00:37:30,840 --> 00:37:31,670
so you don't

870
00:37:31,670 --> 00:37:33,030
have to worry about me.

871
00:37:33,550 --> 00:37:35,070
As for my schedule,

872
00:37:35,070 --> 00:37:36,920
you'll have to be a little flexible.

873
00:37:36,920 --> 00:37:37,670
I usually work

874
00:37:37,670 --> 00:37:39,190
into the early hours of the morning,

875
00:37:39,190 --> 00:37:39,920
okay?

876
00:37:40,920 --> 00:37:43,150
We'll work when it's time to work,

877
00:37:44,510 --> 00:37:46,570
and go on dates when it's time to date.

878
00:37:49,280 --> 00:37:50,150
So...

879
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:52,230
Starting today,

880
00:37:53,400 --> 00:37:55,280
we're authentically...

881
00:37:58,150 --> 00:37:58,960
well,

882
00:37:59,150 --> 00:38:00,510
officially,

883
00:38:01,590 --> 00:38:02,800
I mean officially together.

884
00:38:02,800 --> 00:38:03,930
How does that sound?

885
00:38:08,880 --> 00:38:10,030
Come on.

886
00:38:11,440 --> 00:38:12,510
After everything I just said,

887
00:38:12,510 --> 00:38:13,880
all you're gonna do is nod?

888
00:38:13,880 --> 00:38:15,740
You're supposed to say "mm-hmm".

889
00:38:17,920 --> 00:38:18,630
Mm-hmm.

890
00:38:19,920 --> 00:38:20,630
Mm-hmm!

891
00:38:28,000 --> 00:38:29,400
Why are you staring at me?

892
00:38:33,230 --> 00:38:34,630
Hey, where are you going?

893
00:38:37,230 --> 00:38:38,830
I'll cover it up again later.

894
00:38:38,920 --> 00:38:41,850
But listen, there's something
I need to tell you now.

895
00:38:42,400 --> 00:38:44,800
The light needs to shine
right on your face.

896
00:38:56,280 --> 00:38:56,880
Mom,

897
00:38:56,880 --> 00:38:57,800
your timing

898
00:38:57,800 --> 00:38:58,960
couldn't be better.

899
00:39:02,070 --> 00:39:03,510
Why is Dad making a will?

900
00:39:08,150 --> 00:39:09,150
Right here. Right here.

901
00:39:08,490 --> 00:39:09,990
[Convenience Grocery Store]

902
00:39:09,990 --> 00:39:10,500
[Fucheng Huaide Funeral Center]

903
00:39:10,360 --> 00:39:10,920
Thank you.

904
00:39:10,610 --> 00:39:15,630
[Fucheng Taxi]

905
00:39:15,230 --> 00:39:16,000
You're back.

906
00:39:16,000 --> 00:39:16,710
Zhao.

907
00:39:24,070 --> 00:39:24,920
What's going on?

908
00:39:24,920 --> 00:39:25,650
You're back.

909
00:39:26,960 --> 00:39:28,360
Sweetheart, have a seat.

910
00:39:32,920 --> 00:39:35,000
I had a medical checkup
a couple of days ago,

911
00:39:35,000 --> 00:39:36,760
and they found something seriously wrong.

912
00:39:36,760 --> 00:39:38,030
I want to make a will,

913
00:39:39,480 --> 00:39:41,340
and I'd like you all to witness it.

914
00:39:43,480 --> 00:39:44,740
What's wrong with you?

915
00:39:45,230 --> 00:39:47,590
You'll find out once

916
00:39:49,230 --> 00:39:50,880
I've finished discussing the will.

917
00:39:50,880 --> 00:39:51,680
Don't rush me.

918
00:39:52,000 --> 00:39:53,330
How can I not be worried?

919
00:39:53,840 --> 00:39:55,840
You got the results
and didn't say a word.

920
00:39:55,840 --> 00:39:56,800
What exactly is the illness?

921
00:39:56,800 --> 00:39:57,880
I don't know.

922
00:39:58,280 --> 00:39:59,710
He won't tell us,

923
00:39:59,710 --> 00:40:01,710
and he won't even show us the report.

924
00:40:02,880 --> 00:40:03,670
Amy,

925
00:40:04,920 --> 00:40:05,840
I've got

926
00:40:07,230 --> 00:40:08,320
some savings.

927
00:40:10,320 --> 00:40:11,960
I'll leave them all to you.

928
00:40:14,150 --> 00:40:15,630
As for the shop

929
00:40:16,480 --> 00:40:17,480
and its assets,

930
00:40:17,480 --> 00:40:19,280
you two will split them equally.

931
00:40:19,480 --> 00:40:21,030
Dad, I don't want it.

932
00:40:21,030 --> 00:40:22,190
It should be yours.

933
00:40:25,550 --> 00:40:26,400
And you...

934
00:40:28,400 --> 00:40:29,930
I can't judge who you should

935
00:40:31,030 --> 00:40:34,190
spend the rest of your life with.

936
00:40:34,590 --> 00:40:36,590
But what worries me most is your mom.

937
00:40:37,760 --> 00:40:38,480
You...

938
00:40:39,030 --> 00:40:40,480
Can't you just

939
00:40:40,480 --> 00:40:41,800
-let me finish?
-Have a look please.

940
00:40:41,800 --> 00:40:42,480
Don't worry just yet.

941
00:40:42,480 --> 00:40:43,630
Let me take a look.

942
00:40:45,710 --> 00:40:46,910
Can you see anything?

943
00:40:50,550 --> 00:40:51,880
There's nothing wrong.

944
00:40:52,360 --> 00:40:53,280
What's the matter?

945
00:40:53,280 --> 00:40:54,510
Where exactly is it located?

946
00:40:54,510 --> 00:40:56,320
He's a brain specialist.

947
00:40:56,320 --> 00:40:58,520
How would he know anything about lungs?

948
00:40:59,550 --> 00:41:00,280
The lungs.

949
00:41:01,960 --> 00:41:02,590
Of course I know.

950
00:41:02,590 --> 00:41:03,590
Why wouldn't I?

951
00:41:04,320 --> 00:41:05,030
If you know,

952
00:41:05,030 --> 00:41:06,710
h-how come you couldn't tell?

953
00:41:06,840 --> 00:41:07,900
I can see what it is.

954
00:41:08,190 --> 00:41:08,760
You've got

955
00:41:08,760 --> 00:41:10,360
a lung nodule, right?

956
00:41:10,550 --> 00:41:11,480
It's right here,

957
00:41:11,510 --> 00:41:13,310
about five millimeters across.

958
00:41:13,550 --> 00:41:14,000
Am I right?

959
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:14,920
Exactly!

960
00:41:14,920 --> 00:41:16,450
It's five millimeters now,

961
00:41:16,480 --> 00:41:17,320
but in a year,

962
00:41:17,760 --> 00:41:18,670
or two years,

963
00:41:18,840 --> 00:41:19,960
it'll keep growing,

964
00:41:19,960 --> 00:41:21,840
like a bean

965
00:41:21,840 --> 00:41:23,110
swelling up in water!

966
00:41:23,150 --> 00:41:24,510
Who told you that?

967
00:41:24,760 --> 00:41:26,150
Doctors wouldn't even bother

968
00:41:26,150 --> 00:41:27,810
treating a nodule that small.

969
00:41:27,880 --> 00:41:28,670
They wouldn't bother?

970
00:41:28,670 --> 00:41:29,230
There's nothing wrong with him.

971
00:41:29,230 --> 00:41:29,920
I...

972
00:41:30,030 --> 00:41:31,960
I-I looked it up online.

973
00:41:32,150 --> 00:41:32,670
Dad.

974
00:41:32,670 --> 00:41:33,400
You scared the life out of me.

975
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:35,000
So this "serious illness"

976
00:41:35,320 --> 00:41:36,150
you're talking about is just a nodule?

977
00:41:36,150 --> 00:41:37,360
-That's right.
-I knew it.

978
00:41:37,360 --> 00:41:38,280
You're making a mountain
out of a molehill.

979
00:41:38,280 --> 00:41:39,710
What's that supposed to mean?

980
00:41:39,710 --> 00:41:41,440
A nodule

981
00:41:41,920 --> 00:41:43,880
could turn cancerous even by tomorrow!

982
00:41:43,880 --> 00:41:45,150
Oh, give it a rest.

983
00:41:45,150 --> 00:41:46,280
Don't talk nonsense.

984
00:41:46,280 --> 00:41:47,590
He said there's no need to treat it.

985
00:41:47,590 --> 00:41:48,320
It might not even grow

986
00:41:48,320 --> 00:41:49,360
by the time you're 90.

987
00:41:49,360 --> 00:41:50,510
Y-You're just scaring yourself.

988
00:41:50,510 --> 00:41:52,760
Even if it does grow,
it's easily treatable.

989
00:41:52,760 --> 00:41:53,400
Chen,

990
00:41:53,400 --> 00:41:54,360
stay here and keep Dad company.

991
00:41:54,360 --> 00:41:55,150
I've gotta get back to the internet café.

992
00:41:55,150 --> 00:41:56,030
I've got a bunch of people waiting for me.

993
00:41:56,030 --> 00:41:56,590
Go on, have fun.

994
00:41:56,590 --> 00:41:57,150
I'm off, Chen.

995
00:41:57,150 --> 00:41:57,880
See you.

996
00:41:57,960 --> 00:41:59,000
Wait, but...

997
00:41:59,320 --> 00:42:00,120
this thing...

998
00:42:00,320 --> 00:42:01,590
-I'll continue then.
-You can barely even see it

999
00:42:01,590 --> 00:42:02,510
without a magnifying glass.

1000
00:42:02,510 --> 00:42:03,280
See?

1001
00:42:03,280 --> 00:42:04,000
But

1002
00:42:04,030 --> 00:42:06,150
what if the surgery doesn't go well?

1003
00:42:06,280 --> 00:42:07,760
Who said you need surgery?

1004
00:42:07,760 --> 00:42:08,550
You don't.

1005
00:42:08,880 --> 00:42:10,150
I said what if.

1006
00:42:10,630 --> 00:42:12,560
What if something happens to me...

1007
00:42:14,670 --> 00:42:15,480
Can you two

1008
00:42:15,480 --> 00:42:17,230
let me finish?

1009
00:42:18,760 --> 00:42:19,590
Really.

1010
00:42:26,880 --> 00:42:27,670
Zhengliang,

1011
00:42:28,030 --> 00:42:29,440
from now on, Ai Chen

1012
00:42:29,710 --> 00:42:30,960
is in your care.

1013
00:42:33,030 --> 00:42:34,690
We'll take care of each other.

1014
00:42:37,110 --> 00:42:38,510
Let's go out and celebrate!

1015
00:42:38,510 --> 00:42:39,150
Sounds good!

1016
00:42:39,150 --> 00:42:40,000
What are we eating?

1017
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:40,360
You pick.

1018
00:42:40,360 --> 00:42:41,290
What the heck...

1019
00:42:41,440 --> 00:42:42,190
You decide.

1020
00:42:42,230 --> 00:42:43,190
Don't make him decide.

1021
00:42:43,190 --> 00:42:43,760
It's on us.

1022
00:42:43,760 --> 00:42:44,880
You're still talking about food?

1023
00:42:44,880 --> 00:42:45,630
How about barbecue?

1024
00:42:45,630 --> 00:42:46,320
Barbecue sounds good.

1025
00:42:46,320 --> 00:42:46,960
Barbecue is fine.

1026
00:42:46,960 --> 00:42:48,030
An's restaurant.

1027
00:42:48,030 --> 00:42:48,760
An's restaurant?

1028
00:42:48,760 --> 00:42:50,400
-All right. I'll call... I'll call a car.
-Come on, let's go!

1029
00:42:50,400 --> 00:42:51,320
-Hurry up and call a car.
-Call the car.

1030
00:42:51,320 --> 00:42:52,360
It's always packed there.

1031
00:42:52,360 --> 00:42:53,160
I'm not going.

1032
00:42:54,230 --> 00:42:55,550
Charcoal-grilled food causes cancer.

1033
00:42:55,550 --> 00:42:57,150
All right, then you can stay here
and watch the shop.

1034
00:42:57,150 --> 00:42:59,400
I'll bring you some fresh vegetables
with dipping sauce.

1035
00:42:59,400 --> 00:43:01,550
You probably can't
have the sauce right now, though.

1036
00:43:01,550 --> 00:43:03,030
I'll bring you some oden instead.

1037
00:43:03,030 --> 00:43:03,760
The car's here. Let's go.

1038
00:43:03,760 --> 00:43:04,400
Let's go!

1039
00:43:04,840 --> 00:43:08,000
My mom is the best mom in the world.

1040
00:43:09,360 --> 00:43:10,070
-He...
-He's not going.

1041
00:43:10,070 --> 00:43:10,590
Let's go.

1042
00:43:10,590 --> 00:43:11,550
H-He's really not coming?

1043
00:43:11,550 --> 00:43:12,320
What about the will!
